{
  "archive": "size_declared.qvf",
  "description": "Every member spec carries the optional size, the uncompressed byte count of its ZIP entry (spec \u00a7 4.2): JSON members (structure, bonds, the volume grid, the run.record files index), binary members (the volume data, a vendor int64 array), the opaque citations.references and the run.record input, log and attachment. A validator checks each size against the ZIP central directory before reading the member. The root declares byte_order 'little' (spec \u00a7 2.2). The checks compare the sizes of the binary and opaque members, whose bytes are fixed; a JSON member's size depends on its producer's formatting.",
  "source_program": "qvf-conformance",
